  cutscene_lines:
  - ...
  - 'So you called the police. Perhaps what you witnessed may have been too much
    for you.. '
  - A glimmer of doubt lies behind the corner of your mindscape regarding your decision..
    but surely the authorities could make something out of this situation.. right?
  - ...
  - Damn, they're taking forever to get here.
  - To be fair we're in the middle of god knows where..
  - ( a few minutes later.. )
  - ( police car pulls over )
  - Evening, sir. Ye're Mr. Paul Payton who called in, correct?
  - Yes, officer. It's a bloody whole crime scene in there!
  - Wait, where's the investigation squad?
  - Unfortunately the last investigation unit was assigned on another case in metropolis.
    But don'tcha worry, sir. Another available unit will arrive shortly after.
  - As for now, I have been assigned to secure the perimeter and crime scene before
    they arrive.
  - Also, pleased to meet'cha. Name's Bradley from the police station from the far
    town close to the main city. Say.. how'd ye end up in this desolated house anyway?
    It's miles away..
  - Well I had this hobby of discovering abandoned places, sir. Even the far ones..
  - Curiosity got the better of me as I approached upstairs. That's where I saw the
    blood..
  - I see..
  - Can you show me the location?
  - Yes, officer. Follow me.
  - ...
  - It's over here, officer.
  - Officer?
  - 
  - ( sigh.. )
  - The boss better be true to his word regarding that extra pay..
  - So long, chap.. I'm just doin my job..
  - Trust is a rare gem indeed..
  - Ending 1 - Further Away from Home
